  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Choosing a Load Balancer: ALB, NLB, GWLB",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Choosing a Load Balancer: ALB, NLB, GWLB",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Layers and Jobs",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:ALB} = ==Layer 7==: HTTP, HTTPS, gRPC, WebSocket",
                "ALB routes by **host, path, header, query string**",
                "ALB can authenticate with Cognito or OIDC",
                "{green:NLB} = ==Layer 4==: TCP, UDP, TLS; millions of req/s, ultra-low latency",
                "NLB: one static IP per AZ (Elastic IP optional), keeps **client source IP**",
                "{purple:GWLB} = ==Layer 3==: GENEVE on port `6081`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "sub": "traffic in",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "GWLB",
                    "sub": "transparent",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Appliance fleet",
                    "sub": "firewall, IDS/IPS",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "App",
                    "sub": "after inspection",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Comparison",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "ALB",
                "NLB",
                "GWLB"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Layer",
                  "L7",
                  "L4",
                  "L3"
                ],
                [
                  "Use for",
                  "Smart routing, web apps",
                  "Raw speed, static IPs, PrivateLink",
                  "Inline security appliances"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Only One Can",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Exclusive features",
              "items": [
                "Only ==ALB==: WAF, path/host rules",
                "Only ==NLB==: static / Elastic IPs"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "ALB IPs change",
              "text": "Use the ALB **DNS name**, never hardcode its IPs."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Target Groups and Health Checks",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Target Groups and Health Checks",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Target Groups",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Target group== = the set of targets a listener forwards to",
                "Target types: ==instance==, ==IP==, ==Lambda== (ALB), ==ALB== (as an NLB target)",
                "One target can sit in {blue:several groups}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Health Checks",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Settings: ==protocol==, ==path== (`/health`), ==port==, ==interval==, ==timeout==, success codes (default `200`)",
                "==Healthy / unhealthy threshold== = consecutive passes / fails needed to flip state"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Probe",
                    "sub": "path + port",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fails x threshold",
                    "sub": "unhealthy",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Out of rotation",
                    "sub": "no traffic",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Passes x threshold",
                    "sub": "healthy",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Back in rotation",
                    "sub": "traffic returns",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "All targets unhealthy → LB ==fails open== and routes to all (zonal failover)",
                "A last-resort fallback, {red:not a fix}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Draining and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Deregistration delay== (default `300s`) lets in-flight requests finish",
                "Short requests: lower it, e.g. `30s`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "aws elbv2 modify-target-group-attributes \\",
                "  --target-group-arn <arn> \\",
                "  --attributes Key=deregistration_delay.timeout_seconds,Value=30"
              ],
              "note": "Set the delay to 30 seconds"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Healthy app marked unhealthy",
              "text": "A path needing ==auth== or returning ==301/302== is not `200`. The target security group must also allow the **load balancer's security group**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Listeners, Rules and Routing",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Listeners, Rules and Routing",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Listeners",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Listener== = protocol + port the LB checks for connections",
                "{blue:ALB}: HTTP, HTTPS",
                "{purple:NLB}: TCP, UDP, TLS",
                "HTTPS listener needs an ==ACM certificate=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rules and Actions",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "ALB rule = ==priority== + **conditions** + **action**",
                "Conditions: `host-header`, `path-pattern`, `http-header`, `query-string`, `source-ip`",
                "==Lowest number== is checked first, **default rule** last"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Rule 10",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Rule 20",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Default rule",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Action",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`forward`",
                  "weighted target groups: canary, blue-green"
                ],
                [
                  "`redirect`",
                  "HTTP 80 to HTTPS 443"
                ],
                [
                  "`fixed-response`",
                  "static reply"
                ],
                [
                  "`authenticate-cognito` / `oidc`",
                  "sign-in first"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Create a Rule",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "aws elbv2 create-rule --listener-arn <arn> \\",
                "  --priority 10 \\",
                "  --conditions Field=path-pattern,Values='/api/*' \\",
                "  --actions Type=forward,TargetGroupArn=<arn>"
              ],
              "note": "/api/* goes to one target group"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rule traps",
              "text": "Priorities must be ==unique==. No default action means unmatched requests get **503** or **404**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Auto Scaling Groups and Launch Templates",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Auto Scaling Groups and Launch Templates",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Launch Template: What to Launch",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==AMI==, instance type, key pair, security groups",
                "==IAM instance profile== and **user data**",
                "**Versioned**: point the ASG at `$Latest` or `$Default`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. ASG: How Many and Where",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Capacity}: ==min <= desired <= max==",
                "Subnets across **several AZs**, plus the launch template",
                "Attached **target groups** receive new instances",
                "Health check type ==ELB==, not the default EC2",
                "So instances failing the load balancer check get **replaced**",
                "Set a ==grace period== so boot time is not counted as failure"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Everyday Commands",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "aws autoscaling create-auto-scaling-group --auto-scaling-group-name web \\",
                "  --launch-template LaunchTemplateName=web,Version='$Latest' \\",
                "  --min-size 2 --max-size 6 --desired-capacity 2 \\",
                "  --health-check-type ELB --health-check-grace-period 300",
                "aws autoscaling update-auto-scaling-group --desired-capacity 4",
                "aws autoscaling describe-auto-scaling-instances",
                "aws autoscaling start-instance-refresh  # rolling AMI update"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Templates vs Launch Configurations",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Launch template",
                "Launch configuration"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Status",
                  "{green:Current}",
                  "{red:Deprecated}"
                ],
                [
                  "Editing",
                  "New **versions**",
                  "Cannot be edited"
                ],
                [
                  "Mixed instances + Spot",
                  "==Required==",
                  "Not supported"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Default is EC2",
              "text": "With the default health check type **EC2**, an app failing the ==ELB check== is never replaced."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Scaling Policies, Cooldowns and Multi-AZ, Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Scaling Policies, Cooldowns and Multi-AZ, Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Scaling Policies",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Policy",
                "Trigger",
                "Verdict"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Target tracking",
                  "Pick metric + target",
                  "{green:Best choice}"
                ],
                [
                  "Step scaling",
                  "Alarm + step adjustments",
                  "Good"
                ],
                [
                  "Simple scaling",
                  "Alarm, then cooldown wait",
                  "{red:Avoid}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Target: `ASGAverageCPUUtilization` = ==50%==",
                "For web traffic: ==ALBRequestCountPerTarget==",
                "ASG creates and manages the **alarms**; out fast, in slowly",
                "Step: CloudWatch alarm; CPU 60-70% ==add 1==, above 70% ==add 3=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cooldown and Warmup",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Cooldown== (default 300s) blocks the next simple-scaling action",
                "Target tracking and step use ==instance warmup==, a separate setting",
                "Warmup keeps new instances out of metrics until ready"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Multi-AZ and Cheat Sheet",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Subnets in ==2+ AZs==",
                "ASG balances evenly; rebalances after AZ failure or recovery",
                "Cross-zone: ALB ==on==, NLB ==off== by default"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Item",
                "Value"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "ALB / NLB / GWLB",
                  "L7 routing / L4 speed + static IP / L3 appliances"
                ],
                [
                  "Health check type",
                  "==ELB=="
                ],
                [
                  "Deregistration delay",
                  "300s: in-flight requests finish before removal"
                ],
                [
                  "Capacity",
                  "min <= desired <= max"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Prefer",
              "text": "Target tracking on ==ALBRequestCountPerTarget==; simple scaling stalls for the cooldown after every action."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An app on an ASG instance crashes, but the instance keeps running. The ALB marks it unhealthy. The ASG health check type is the default. What happens?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Nothing: the default type `EC2` only checks the instance, so the ASG never replaces it.",
                "Set the health check type to `ELB`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "The health check path is `/admin`, which returns a 302 to a login page. What happens to the targets?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The default success code is 200, so every healthy target is marked unhealthy.",
                "With all targets unhealthy, the load balancer fails open and routes to all of them.",
                "Use a public `/health` path that returns 200."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Rule priority 10 is `/api/*` to group A. Priority 20 is `/api/v2/*` to group B. Where does `/api/v2/users` go?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Group A: the lowest number is evaluated first and `/api/*` matches.",
                "Give the specific rule the lower number."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}